<title>SINGAPORE: IOC tenders to buy October 0.25 sulphur diesel.</title>
<headline>IOC tenders to buy October 0.25 sulphur diesel.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has issued a tender to buy two 0.25 percent high speed diesel cargoes for delivery to the west coast, industry sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The tender calls for the delivery of one 45,000-tonne cargo each on October 11-15 and October 21-25. The tender closes on September 12 with validity to September 13.</p>
<p>IOC had bought two cargoes in September, one from a U.S. major at mean of MidEast quotes plus $2.88 cost and freight (c-and-f) Kandla and the other from a Mideast state oil producer at 90 cents free on board (fob) Kuwat.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (65-870-3093)</p>
